                <pb facs="0347" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 788/70–76.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Straight to the Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. D 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirming my cipher telegram of the
                    20th instant as follows,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d197-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy of my dispatch No. 105, of even date, to the legation
                    at Peking, as well as the inclosures therewith, excepting the Chinese texts,
                    regarding the agreement above mentioned.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard D.
                    Straight.</hi></signed></closer>








